                <pb facs="0830" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg782"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that it has been decided on our part to make Osaka
                    a port of entry, as soon as an agreement to that effect shall have been made
                    with the foreign representatives.</p>
                <p>I also have to notify you that, even if the representatives should desire it now
                    or hereafter, Yedo cannot become a port of entry, and that it is intended to
                    open it as a city. The 28th day of the 5th month, (17th July.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HIGASHI KUZE CHIRIJIO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Valkenburgh</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
